  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sanitation for Women and Men with Disabilities</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This aim of this project is to supply assistance to the disabled members of society in Bangladesh.

In Bangladesh, sanitation and hygiene facilities for disabled people have not been fully addressed, which has severe consequences for the health, dignity, education and employment of disabled people and their caregivers. 

ADD aims to reach disabled people in Faridpur and Bagerhat districts, they will receive house hold (HH) based sanitation facilities, community based facilities and community awareness raising and self-help group (SHG) meetings. 

Further 8,000 people will be reached indirectly: family members of the direct project participants, local government authorities, school teachers and students, N/GOs working on WATSAN intervention and through watsan networks. The project intervention also includes awareness raising of the disabled person&#x2019;s right to sanitation and advocacy to implement the national law on inclusive sanitation and hygiene as a right for all existing SHGs at grassroots level. 
CAFOD partner Bangladesh University for Engineering and Technology (ITN-BUET) will provide technical support to ADD for developing disable friendly sanitation equipment and will provide community latrines to disabled people. Disabled friendly WASH facilities and equipment include varying sizes of seated commode with pan, commode with hand/leg stands and body supports, hand supports, bed latrine, rails and ramps.</narrative>
  </description>
